A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per problem and merge
reports that share a cause, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate when its **cause** matches the cause of an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), which replaces
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):

1. look up the report's tenant: its locale and its booking form;
2. work out the cause from them, not from the subject line or the intake tag;
3. look for an open ticket with the same cause and merge into it. None: open a new ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
A matching subject is not enough. In #4471 the same subjects covered three different problems.
See [what it holds](/kb/incidents/4471-three-problems).
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the reports apart and read the body. A ticket you merge wrongly hides a problem, and splitting it later
costs more than a second ticket.
